# Two stale copies of an older privacy policy, published before /privacy/
# existed and byte-identical to each other. Nothing on this site links to
# either, but an app store listing or a saved link might, so they are not
# deleted — a privacy policy URL that 404s is worse than one that moves.
# A permanent redirect keeps those links working, sends anyone who follows
# one to the policy that is actually current, and leaves search engines with
# a single canonical copy instead of three.
/privacy-policy       /privacy/   301
/privacy-policy.html  /privacy/   301
/PRIVACY_POLICY       /privacy/   301
/PRIVACY_POLICY.html  /privacy/   301

# The brand set before the October 2026 identity. /media/* is served
# immutable for a year, so the new set lives under its own folder rather than
# reusing these names, and a returning visitor cannot keep the old logo. These
# keep any outside link to an old file working, and show it the new one.
